{
  "schemaVersion": "capability-objects-v1",
  "$comment": [
    "THE OBJECT AXIS. ONE EVERYDAY VOCABULARY PER NAMESPACE.",
    "",
    "A namespace IS the object: `gmail` is email, `screen` is the screen,",
    "`workspace` is the other computer. This file says what a PERSON calls that",
    "thing, which is frequently not what the code calls it -- nobody types",
    "'gmail', they type 'inbox'; nobody types 'host', they type 'my computer'.",
    "",
    "This is the real authoring in the system, and it is the part that cannot be",
    "derived: the gap between a namespace name and a person's word for it is",
    "exactly the knowledge a lexicon exists to carry. Everything else (the verb,",
    "the read/write split, the tool's own description) comes from the catalogue.",
    "",
    "`says` are NOUNS -- the thing. Verbs live in actions.json and compose with",
    "these. 'read my email' is action:read x object:gmail, and neither half",
    "needed to know about the other.",
    "",
    "A namespace with no entry FAILS THE BUILD. That is the anti-rot rule: a new",
    "namespace added by another lane cannot ship with no way for a person to",
    "name it."
  ],
